E. Robust Proximal Policy Optimization
To solve the outer maximization with generated optimal adversaries, and learn the robust optimal driving policy, we introduce a robust proximal policy optimization in this section. We adopt PPO as our baseline DRL. It is a model-free, onpolicy, stochastic method. It shares the similar idea of TRPO (Trust Region Policy Optimization) algorithm [29], which restricts the policy update based on the probability ratio or the KL divergence between the new policy and the old policy. The most popular PPO variant employs a clipped surrogate objective to prevent the new policy differing too much from the old policy:

Lclip(π) = Eˆt[min((rt(π), clip(rt(π), 1 − ε, 1 + ε))Aˆt)] (5)

