V. CONCLUSION
In this paper, we introduce a novel approach for deep reinforcement learning based robust autonomous driving against observation perturbation with an explainable adversarial detection model. The realm of autonomous driving and decisionmaking models based on deep reinforcement learning is constantly challenged by safety issues arising from inevitable sen-

sor failures or transitions between domains. These challenges bear a resemblance to adversarial attacks, as they potentially disrupt or compromise the agent’s ability to make accurate decisions in critical situations. To approximate the worst-case perturbation, we develop a white-box optimal method for generating adversaries, which has full access to the parameters of the RL agent model, enabling the creation of training samples for robust reinforcement learning. This method is based on fast gradient sign method (FGSM), incorporating with our collision risk maximum formulation. To more efficiently attack the RL agent, we use iteration on FGSM rather than simply enlarge the attack strength parameter ε to reduce the visibility of the adversarial examples. After obtaining the perturbated observation, we introduce a Markov decision process with perturbation to formulate the urban roundabout making for autonomous driving under constraint observation uncertainties. Furthermore, a divergence based optimization term is applied to mimic the performance gap between non-adversarial states and adversarial states. An adversarial attack detection network based on explainable saliency map is also introduced to enhance our understanding of the fundamental decision-making processes in the presence of adversarial attacks.
We conduct experiments for each of the three components within our approach. The results demonstrate the notably high attack success rate achieved by our proposed method when applied to the well-trained baseline model. Furthermore, our proposed robust agent shows resilient and robust performance under such strong perturbation across various evaluation conditions. Moreover, our detection model attains high accuracy in detecting attacks and offers comprehensive visualizations,

